// ============================================================================
// BILL OF MATERIALS (BOM)
// ============================================================================

SEMICONDUCTORS:
- 2N3904 NPN ............................................. 20 pcs
- 2N2222 NPN (optional for dot driver) .................... 2 pcs

PASSIVES:
- Resistors:
  - 1 MΩ .................................................. 1
  - 100 kΩ ................................................ 10
  - 47 kΩ ................................................. 10
  - 10 kΩ ................................................. 20
  - 4.7 kΩ ................................................ 15
  - 1–2.2 kΩ .............................................. 5

- Capacitors:
  - 22–33 pF (crystal load) ............................... 2
  - 1 nF (divider shaping) ................................ 4
  - 1 µF .................................................. 4
  - 2.2 µF ................................................ 2
  - 3.3 µF ................................................ 2
  - 4.7 µF ................................................ 4
  - 6.8 µF ................................................ 2
  - 8.2 µF ................................................ 2
  - 10 µF ................................................. 4

TIMING SOURCE:
- 3.579545 MHz NTSC crystal ............................... 1

MCU:
- ATtiny85 / Arduino Nano / similar ....................... 1
- Jumper wires ............................................ assorted

OUTPUT:
- CRT video input pad OR LED + resistor ................... 1


// ============================================================================
// WIRING CHECKLIST (MARK OFF AS YOU BUILD)
// ============================================================================

STAGE 1 — MASTER OSCILLATOR (Q1)
- [ ] Crystal between collector ↔ base node
- [ ] 1 MΩ collector → base
- [ ] 100 kΩ base → ground
- [ ] Two 22–33 pF caps from crystal ends → ground
- [ ] 10 kΩ collector → +5 V
- [ ] Output labeled CRYSTAL_OSC_OUT

STAGE 2 — DIVIDER CHAIN (Q2–Q5)
For each divider stage:
- [ ] 10 kΩ collector → +5 V
- [ ] 47 kΩ base resistor from previous stage
- [ ] 1 nF shaping cap → ground
- [ ] Outputs labeled:
      FR_30, FR_100, FR_1000, FIELD_SYNC, PHASE_CLK

STAGE 3 — MODE SELECTOR (QM1–QM3)
- [ ] QM1 collector → FR_30
- [ ] QM2 collector → FR_100
- [ ] QM3 collector → FR_1000
- [ ] Emitters → ground
- [ ] Collectors OR’d → FRAME_CLK_OUT
- [ ] MCU MODE_0 / MODE_1 → bases via 4.7–10 kΩ

STAGE 4 — ILLUSION CLASS SELECTOR (QC0–QC6)
RC networks:
- [ ] L0: 100 kΩ + 10 µF
- [ ] L1: 100 kΩ + 8.2 µF
- [ ] L2: 100 kΩ + 6.8 µF
- [ ] L3: 100 kΩ + 4.7 µF
- [ ] L4: 47 kΩ + 3.3 µF
- [ ] L5: 47 kΩ + 2.2 µF
- [ ] L6: 47 kΩ + 1 µF
Selector:
- [ ] QCx collectors → PW_Lx_NODE
- [ ] QCx emitters → PULSE_CTRL_OUT
- [ ] MCU CLASS_0/1/2 → base decode

STAGE 5 — PROFILE SELECTOR (QP0–QP3)
Envelope RC networks:
- [ ] Breathing: 100 kΩ + 10 µF
- [ ] Drift: 100 kΩ + 4.7–10 µF
- [ ] Ghostwave: 47 kΩ + 4.7 µF
- [ ] Whiteout: 10 kΩ + 1 µF
Selector:
- [ ] QP0–QP3 collectors → envelope nodes
- [ ] Emitters → LUMA_ENV_IN
- [ ] MCU PROFILE_0/1 → base decode

STAGE 6 — DOT DRIVER (QD1)
- [ ] QD1 base → (PULSE_CTRL_OUT + LUMA_ENV_IN) via 4.7 kΩ
- [ ] QD1 emitter → ground
- [ ] QD1 collector → CRT video input through 1–2.2 kΩ
- [ ] OR LED + resistor if using LED dot

STAGE 7 — MCU HOOK
- [ ] PIN_FIELD_SYNC → FIELD_SYNC node via 10 kΩ
- [ ] MODE_0 / MODE_1 → mode selector bases
- [ ] CLASS_0 / CLASS_1 / CLASS_2 → class selector bases
- [ ] PROFILE_0 / PROFILE_1 → profile selector bases
- [ ] MCU ground → analog ground
- [ ] MCU +5 V → analog +5 V

FINAL POWER‑ON CHECK:
- [ ] All grounds common
- [ ] +5 V stable
- [ ] Oscillator running
- [ ] Divider taps present
- [ ] MCU receiving FIELD_SYNC
- [ ] Dot driver connected
- [ ] No floating selector bases
- [ ] No shorted RC networks

